{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Read a page of postalref.com"},"description":"Read a page of postalref.com by its path. /glossary/<id> gives what USPS means by a term: its entry, with its kind and tier, the USPS words that define it and the page they're on, its other names, postalref's own explanation where it has one, and when USPS ended or renamed it, each with USPS's words; /glossary/<words>, such as /glossary/mailer-id or /glossary/MID, gives the entries those words name, in the order search ranks them. /codes/<table>/<code>, such as /codes/service-type-codes/055, gives a code's row as USPS prints it in the newest edition that lists it, the editions that list it and its history. /documents/<id> gives any document postalref holds, page by page as extracted, to quote, and /documents lists them. Any other path is a page of the site, given as its Markdown: a product page (/products/<id>), a guide (/guides/<id>), a code table's home (/codes/<table>), a case (/cases/<id>), a spec (/specs/<id>), a topic (/topics/<id>) or /changes. Quote whole sentences, word for word. A definition's words cite its document and page, and its `read` names the document and page to read for the sentences around them. A document's `text`, or a `found` context, which shows the whole sentence around the words or the lead-in with the list it opens, cites the revision's sha256, the PDF page and the words exactly; read another page `found` lists by its `pdf` number, or a part by its number, as `page`. When the text ends mid-sentence or mid-list, `continued` gives the rest of it from `next`, cited by its own page; when it ends mid-table, or a list goes on past `continued`, read `next`. A text without pages, a web page or a product page, reads in parts, and a quote from one cites no page.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"find":{"description":"With /documents/<id>: words to find, as one phras